1
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:18,440
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and let
it fly until it gets there.

3
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:29,360
To the kashiwa of the joking type,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
they laughed at me for staying
just as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
it's serious,
there's only one way to hold it.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,020
One nightmare that never changes.

8
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:43,880
The townscape is gentler somehow.

9
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing.

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,980
It's already getting dark, isn't it.

11
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:53,820
Are you going to look at
the authentic yakitori stalls?

12
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:57,500
With the pointed hat...

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,620
Measured out in great stretches by people...

14
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:04,080
The setting sun falls.

15
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:10,080
Looks like I'll end up losing tomorrow too

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,700
A magazine, maybe?
"Happiness again," they say.

17
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,660
I took the easy way and realized it.

18
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm such a fool.

19
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:29,880
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

20
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:32,420
Well, if it isn't Honda.

21
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:33,640
Hello there.

22
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:35,560
What do you want, Honda?

23
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,940
Well, I just stopped by the
bookstore a little while ago, and...

24
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:41,100
Weekly Sapphire was out,
so I picked up a copy.

25
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,800
Come on, let me see it.

26
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:46,000
My Robodeka Banchou...

27
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,300
Ryo-chan, it's still being serialized?

28
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:49,860
Of course it is.

29
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:52,760
Robodeka Banchou is our flagship manga,
after all.

30
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:54,820
It's not gone, you know.

31
00:01:54,820 --> 00:01:56,800
My Robodeka Banchou...

32
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:58,220
isn't in it?

33
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:04,240
No. Didn't you forget to send the manuscript?
No way, that's not it.

34
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:09,840
I sent it properly! Aaaah!
Senpai, look here, right here!

35
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,040
Here!

36
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,540
What?!

37
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:19,260
Ryotsu-ryū Manga Juku

38
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:29,340
That Dragon Warrior bastard!
Cancelling my manga without permission!

39
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,980
I won't forgive this! Step on it, Honda!

40
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:33,140
Alright!

41
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:40,200
Hey, Dragon Warrior!
What the hell is the meaning of this!

42
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,500
G-good to see you, Patricia Kanko-sensei.

43
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:46,280
I'd like to hear your
explanation thoroughly.

44
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:49,660
Y-yes, we can't talk here.
Let's go to the reception room.

45
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:51,320
Mm, so?

46
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,120
First,

47
00:02:55,180 --> 00:02:55,940
please take a look at this.

48
00:02:56,860 --> 00:02:57,680
This is...

49
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:01,160
These are the results of last
week's reader popularity poll.

50
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:05,580
Wow! Nana-chan's Mediette
is in first place! Yes!

51
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:08,160
And my Robodeka Banchou...

52
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:10,380
Last place!

53
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:13,060
I mean, it didn't get a single vote...

54
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:16,220
B-but even if it was last place just once...

55
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:18,120
No, not just once.

56
00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:20,740
This is the reader poll for
the last 100 installments.

57
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:23,900
Look closely at the last-place spot, okay?

58
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:33,360
Wow, amazing.
Only last place never budges an inch.

59
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:38,032
As you can see,

60
00:03:38,082 --> 00:03:41,460
Robodeka Banchou has been last
for 100 installments in a row.

61
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:43,500
B-but...

62
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:47,500
Well, if it were just unpopular,
that would be one thing.

63
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,360
No...

64
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:51,320
We've also been getting
complaint postcards from readers.

65
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:52,980
S-this many?

66
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:55,740
No, this is just a fraction of them.

67
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:58,160
There are about fifteen
more boxes in the storehouse.

68
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:03,060
Mm...

69
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:04,820
Er er...

70
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:05,760
So, as it turns out,

71
00:04:06,210 --> 00:04:10,440
at last week's editorial meeting, it was
decided that Robodeka Banchou will be cancelled.

72
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:12,320
Do you have some complaint?

73
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:14,280
I get it.

74
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:17,640
O-kay, you understand now?

75
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:18,172
Yeah,

76
00:04:18,222 --> 00:04:23,160
I've actually been feeling that
Robodeka Banchou has been stale lately,

77
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:25,420
so let's just end it cleanly and decisively.

78
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:28,380
I see, I'm glad you understand.

79
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,960
In its place, let's start a new serial.

80
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,780
W-what, a new serial?

81
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:37,920
I said "mm," and it came right away, so...

82
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:39,760
Done, there we go!

83
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:42,600
Wow, finished it in five minutes!

84
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,660
Here, go read it.

85
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:47,620
What kind of manga is it?

86
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:51,220
This time, it's a completely
different style from Robodeka Banchou,

87
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:56,780
a hardboiled gekiga gag action series
set in the port city of Yokohama.

88
00:04:56,780 --> 00:04:58,860
My gun is calling me!

89
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:02,780
Hardboiled gekiga, gag art by James Rihotz.

90
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,340
Bo~

91
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:06,040
Hyoon, hyoon!

92
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:07,820
This one's got a role for you.

93
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:10,160
Alright, let's buy it for a billion yen.

94
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:11,380
We're both bad guys

95
00:05:12,220 --> 00:05:14,240
I can't beat the boss, aru.

96
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:16,240
Not so fast, Kintaro-hame!

97
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:16,780
Crunch.

98
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:17,680
Daruda.

99
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:19,240
Ta-da!

100
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,720
I'm no dandy from Pyokkori Pyotan Island,
you know!

101
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:29,220
Boss-san, this is serious, aru yo.

102
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:32,380
Hey, you bastards, Jo, take 'em out!

103
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:33,600
Woooah!

104
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:36,120
Take Jo's rapid-fire barrage,
one after another!

105
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,040
Whoa!

106
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:40,800
T-this, for Weekly Sapphire...

107
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:43,560
How about that?
It's so funny your jaw drops, right?

108
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,880
Especially the ending,
the ending is the best!

109
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:46,560
The ending?

110
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:48,560
If they don't spit up blood, that's a lie!

111
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,980
I don't know, aru yo.

112
00:05:49,980 --> 00:05:53,480
Detective Tondobayasu,
this isn't narcotics, it's flour!

113
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:57,660
Gaaah! I told you it wasn't, aru yo!

114
00:05:57,880 --> 00:06:00,340
I only bought flour for ten billion yen!

115
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:03,740
Oh no, Tondobayasu-kun,
what is the meaning of this!

116
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:05,680
Oops, my apologies again!

117
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:08,960
Sui sui sui, dararatta sui-kan!

118
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:12,360
How's that for an unexpected twist.

119
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:15,220
Even a top-class writer couldn't
come up with that punchline, right?

120
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:19,260
But why are the people who aren't
the culprit holding machine guns?

121
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:24,080
Gulp... well, that's because a machine gun
just happened to be lying in the port warehouse.

122
00:06:24,080 --> 00:06:27,120
Then the protagonist showed
up just as he picked it up.

123
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:29,660
The protagonist is shooting
the opponent dead, though.

124
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:33,660
Gulp, yeah, yeah, the opponent just
happened to be wearing a bulletproof vest.

125
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:35,060
So it's a weapon, a weapon.

126
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:36,760
Everyone's getting shot in the head, though.

127
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:40,060
That's why they're wearing
bulletproof wigs, see.

128
00:06:40,060 --> 00:06:43,560
Buying plain flour at such
a high price is unnatural too.

129
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:47,300
Yeah, would anyone really go all the way
to the port to pull off something like this?

130
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:55,380
It just doesn't flow well, you know. Ugh, you're so annoying, nitpicking everything.
It's a gag manga, so just let the small details slide.

131
00:06:55,780 --> 00:07:04,160
Either way, this manga isn't suited for Weekly Sapphire.
We can't run it. Please, don't try to talk your way around this.

132
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:11,780
No way. In any case, Ryo-san's manga
can never be run in Weekly Sapphire again.

133
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:14,820
This was decided at the editorial meeting.

134
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:20,840
Curse you!

135
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:25,000
If it's hopeless,
then you'd better give up gracefully.

136
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:27,200
What are you talking about?
Giving up that easily?

137
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:29,360
Stop it, Honda!

138
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:32,820
Hey, what's going on, Honda-san?

139
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:34,140
Look, over there.

140
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:38,660
There sure are a lot of
books thrown away here.

141
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:41,340
This is the place of the
old man at Sekine Publishing.

142
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:44,820
Why are there so many
books thrown away here?

143
00:07:45,140 --> 00:07:46,720
They still look brand new, though.

144
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:50,260
They're not thrown away, you know.

145
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:52,520
It's you, old man. You're here?

146
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:55,340
These are all books
that were returned to us.

147
00:07:55,340 --> 00:07:56,300
All of these?

148
00:07:56,780 --> 00:07:58,420
It's not just the outside.

149
00:07:58,420 --> 00:08:00,280
Inside too, it's a mountain of weird books

150
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:02,900
Still, what an enormous amount.

151
00:08:02,900 --> 00:08:04,820
It's the publishing slump, after all.

152
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:07,020
What kind of books did you make, anyway?

153
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:09,380
"The World's Pen Nibs"

154
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,680
"Faucet Encyclopedia"

155
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:14,960
"The Wonderful World of Bolts and Nuts"

156
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:17,500
There's no way that'll sell!

157
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:19,320
R-really?

158
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:20,920
It definitely won't sell!

159
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:22,100
I guarantee it.

160
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:23,320
So it really is like that

161
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:27,160
We have to make a book that sells,
or we're in trouble.

162
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:29,620
At this rate, we're going bankrupt.

163
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:33,260
A book that sells a book that sells.

164
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:35,280
Then it's a manga!

165
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:36,420
Manga?

166
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:39,280
That's it!
All we need to do is make a manga magazine!

167
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:41,340
Even though you're small,

168
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:43,840
as a publishing company president,
you should know this!

169
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,935
In this publishing slump,

170
00:08:45,985 --> 00:08:48,560
the only thing selling well is,
precisely, manga!

171
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:53,860
Manga is widely read, mainly by young people,
from children to adults.

172
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:57,680
Plus it's cheap,
and you can read it anytime, anywhere.

173
00:08:57,680 --> 00:08:59,800
Above all, the content is interesting.

174
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:04,060
If we put out a manga magazine,
Dad's crisis can be overcome.

175
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:05,060
I see.

176
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,400
But it's impossible.

177
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:10,260
I have no know-how for
making a manga magazine,

178
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:12,240
and I don't know any manga artists.

179
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:21,100
Leave it all to me. A popular manga artist's series just ended,
so he's free right now.

180
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:28,240
That's it, Senpai. You're not planning to serialize your own manga, are you?
Of course. Just as I thought.

181
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:37,080
There, done in four minutes this time! This is
my masterpiece. What do you think? It's a book!

182
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:47,300
This is a sequel to Robodeka Banchou, which
ended while it was still hugely popular.

183
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:57,400
Robodeka Banchou got an anime adaptation too, so it's extremely well known.
It would be a waste to let it end like that, so I've decided to bring it back in a new magazine.

184
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,201
B-but Senpai,

185
00:09:59,251 --> 00:10:02,400
what about the manga artists other than you?

186
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,940
Just ask the publisher, right?

187
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:09,280
Hello? Is this the Weekly
Step editorial department?

188
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:12,600
Who's your most popular manga artist?

189
00:10:13,760 --> 00:10:17,320
Seiko? Good.
Give me that person's phone number.

190
00:10:18,060 --> 00:10:18,880
The reason?

191
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:21,680
Of course, so he can draw for our magazine.

192
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:24,580
Uh...

193
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:29,080
Damn it, hanging up on me like that.
What a rude guy.

194
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:31,640
You're the rude one, senpai.

195
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:32,380
What?

196
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:36,840
Popular manga artists are assets to a publisher,
you know.

197
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:39,800
Information about manga
artists is top secret.

198
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:41,120
Damn it!

199
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,620
Ryo-san, it's probably hopeless after all...

200
00:10:43,620 --> 00:10:45,400
Don't you dare give up!

201
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:48,340
We're launching a manga
magazine no matter what.

202
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:49,900
But how?

203
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,800
There must be some way.

204
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:52,680
Some way...

205
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:58,760
That's it. We'll just have a good artist draw
manga that looks just like a famous writer's.

206
00:11:00,940 --> 00:11:04,440
Hey, Ryo-san, isn't that a bit too risky?

207
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:07,360
Paintings have replicas, don't they?

208
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,960
There's no reason manga can't have them too.

209
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:13,360
I don't think paintings
and manga are the same thing.

210
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:17,420
And what if the real author sues us?

211
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:22,200
Don't worry, that's my specialty.

212
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:26,120
If they sue, I'm confident I can talk my
way out of it and claim they copied us.

213
00:11:27,700 --> 00:11:30,720
But how will we find skilled artists?

214
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:35,100
I have a plan.

215
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:47,140
A manga school

216
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:50,100
The students write
manuscripts as assignments,

217
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:51,980
and we publish them in the magazine.

218
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:54,560
That way,
we don't have to pay manuscript fees.

219
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:57,380
We use the manga school's
tuition and material fees

220
00:11:57,380 --> 00:11:59,340
to cover printing and binding costs,

221
00:11:59,340 --> 00:12:00,900
so we can make books for free!

222
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:02,680
I see, that's amazing.

223
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,200
It's the magical business method!

224
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:08,240
But will students actually come in, though?

225
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:10,220
Don't worry about that part.

226
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:12,760
We've also invited
special guest instructors.

227
00:12:13,220 --> 00:12:15,320
Jackie Ponchi-sensei,

228
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,480
Horolika Kazuyoshi-sensei,

229
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,940
and Nana-chan too.

230
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:18,620
No, no, that's not it.

231
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:20,120
Take a good look.

232
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,780
Ai no Miko-sensei...

233
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:26,920
Her ex-boyfriend... could that be me?

234
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:28,420
Ding-dong!

235
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:32,780
I'm not joking! I can't draw manga at all.

236
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:36,040
Besides, we're still dating.
We're not ex-anything.

237
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:37,940
Don't mind, don't mind.

238
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:41,000
So, maybe other people too...

239
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:45,440
the former housekeeper
of Jackie Ponchi-sensei,

240
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:48,860
and the housewife of
Horolika Kazuyoshi-sensei...

241
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:50,780
Great...

242
00:12:56,900 --> 00:12:58,300
The teacher's about to come in.

243
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:00,020
I wonder if Ai-no-Sensei will come.

244
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,620
Look at all these people, Ryo-san.

245
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:04,700
The special instructors are here

246
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:08,940
Now, we will begin the lecture
by our special instructors.

247
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:10,980
We've been waiting for this!

248
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:12,240
It's Ai-no-Sensei!

249
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:12,860
He's here!

250
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,440
What?

251
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:18,360
Ai-no-Sensei is a man?!

252
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:29,480
Ai-no-Sensei's real name
is Nana Otohime-chan.

253
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:33,200
This is the purikura we took together.

254
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:40,060
This is a photo from when we
went touring the other day.

255
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:42,140
That's a different man from before.

256
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:42,900
Really.

257
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:43,800
She's two-timing.

258
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:44,800
That's all.

259
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:49,100
What is this?

260
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:50,780
What was she trying to say?

261
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:54,840
So, Ai-no-Sensei's real
name is Otohime Nana,

262
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:58,100
which means she's dating two men, isn't it?

263
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:01,720
Do you think that was good enough?

264
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:03,060
That's excellent.

265
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,980
Leave the rest to me.

266
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,680
Hello, Shagun

267
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,680
I'm John Ryotsu, your full-time instructor.

268
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:18,220
Nice to meet you.

269
00:14:20,420 --> 00:14:21,840
if I enroll at this school,

270
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:24,440
it said I'd definitely become a pro.

271
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:25,560
Don't worry.

272
00:14:26,180 --> 00:14:27,900
If you do exactly as I say,

273
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:30,780
you'll debut as a pro, 100%.

274
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:31,760
Is that so?

275
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:32,520
Good.

276
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:35,780
Since I'm here,

277
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:38,580
you can rest easy,
as if you're on a great ship.

278
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:41,020
Now, let's begin the lesson.

279
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:43,360
First, prepare your paper.

280
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:52,360
I brought mine, but Mom said no,
so I'm using the school-designated paper.

281
00:14:54,160 --> 00:15:01,220
If you want to become a pro, you need to use good paper too.
I get that good manga can't be drawn without it, but -

282
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:07,200
It's like drawing paper at 500 yen or 10 yen a sheet.
No, that's not it.

283
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:11,080
And everyone buys the teaching materials.

284
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:13,300
They're absolutely
necessary to become a pro.

285
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:15,380
That's expensive. Eighty thousand yen?

286
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:17,520
A single pencil for 1,000 yen?!

287
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:19,340
Do they really use protractors?

288
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:20,580
Screwdrivers too.

289
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:23,920
They're all wonderful
items I carefully selected.

290
00:15:23,920 --> 00:15:26,100
Screentone for 100 yen?

291
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:28,640
So we can buy the teacher's tone cheaply.

292
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:31,260
That's right,
it's a bargain only for students.

293
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:33,700
Then I'll take ten sheets of number 61.

294
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:34,980
Me too.

295
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:36,180
I'll take twenty of these.

296
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:39,440
It's this small?

297
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:41,400
Stick it on the small part.

298
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:42,900
It's like a postage stamp.

299
00:15:43,340 --> 00:15:46,480
I've also prepared other necessities
you'll need as professionals.

300
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:48,760
Be sure to buy them.

301
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:50,300
T-that's expensive!

302
00:15:50,300 --> 00:15:52,380
Drawing one work costs 100,000 yen.

303
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:54,960
Manga artists have to have drawing skills.

304
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:58,440
That's why I'm handing out
drawing dolls to you all now.

305
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:02,240
A drawing doll, Dessan-kun No. 1.

306
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:04,720
It looks like a cursed straw doll.

307
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:07,860
It's a marvel,
with wire inside so it moves freely.

308
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:10,660
Next, the female figure drawing doll,
Model 325.

309
00:16:10,660 --> 00:16:12,240
It's exactly the same.

310
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:15,120
There's also a horse drawing doll.

311
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:16,480
It's like the Obon festival.

312
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:19,580
Now, I'll finally teach you
the basics of storytelling.

313
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:20,280
Sensei.

314
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:25,220
I brought a piece I drew myself.
Could you take a look?

315
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,120
Very well.

316
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:31,160
I tried to make an artistic piece with love for humanity as the theme,
at least.

317
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:32,680
What do you think?

318
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:38,560
Theme? Art?
Readers don't want that kind of thing!

319
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:41,340
That's just the author's self-indulgence,
satisfying only themselves.

320
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:44,760
What readers want to read is,
above all else, manga that's fun.

321
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:46,160
Can't you even understand that?

322
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:48,160
Yes, sorry about that.

323
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:51,600
So what exactly makes a manga fun?

324
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:54,140
I'll teach you the secret now.

325
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:56,900
First, shonen manga.

326
00:16:57,660 --> 00:17:01,380
The basic shonen manga protagonist
is a bit of a delinquent type.

327
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,760
And right beside him, a beautiful heroine.

328
00:17:05,210 --> 00:17:07,480
Plus, the protagonist's... old-fashioned...

329
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:12,080
And the protagonist always needs an enemy.

330
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:15,280
The stronger the enemy, the better.

331
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:18,840
That way, the joy when the
protagonist defeats them is greater.

332
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:24,000
And now,
the long-awaited showdown with the enemy!

333
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:27,020
The hero and the enemy
must always have a showdown.

334
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:30,760
Whatever you do,
the hero must not defeat the enemy here.

335
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:35,440
He must be beaten by
the enemy at least once.

336
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:40,360
And the hero keenly
feels his own powerlessness

337
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:42,900
and sheds at least a
few tears of frustration.

338
00:17:43,860 --> 00:17:45,120
And then, special training!

339
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:45,920
Special training.

340
00:17:45,920 --> 00:17:50,880
Usually in this situation, the hero holes up
in the mountains and stands under a waterfall.

341
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:56,540
Then he repeats training upon training
and comes up with a new technique.

342
00:17:56,540 --> 00:18:00,960
It's even better if he shaves off one of his own
eyebrows so he can't run away from the mountain.

343
00:18:01,380 --> 00:18:03,911
And then, another showdown with the enemy...

344
00:18:03,961 --> 00:18:07,920
Here, you build it up as much as possible,
and finally defeat the enemy.

345
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:13,311
Then the former enemy is moved
by the hero's personal charm,

346
00:18:13,361 --> 00:18:15,460
and becomes the hero's ally.

347
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:19,700
But by then, a dark shadow is
already creeping up on them.

348
00:18:20,300 --> 00:18:22,280
A new enemy appears.

349
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:23,540
And that's how it goes.

350
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:26,901
Enemy appears, confrontation,

351
00:18:26,951 --> 00:18:28,910
defeat, training,

352
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,890
confrontation, victory,

353
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:33,580
reconciliation, and another enemy appears.

354
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:38,160
As long as you keep repeating this,
you can keep a shonen manga going forever.

355
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:39,900
So that's how it is!

356
00:18:40,860 --> 00:18:41,660
Sensei?

357
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:42,160
What is it?

358
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:45,380
I want to draw shoujo manga, though.

359
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:48,200
Shoujo manga Very well.

360
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:50,560
When it comes to shoujo manga,
it's all about romance.

361
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:53,680
The basic setup is the heroine falling
for a boy who transfers to her school.

362
00:18:53,680 --> 00:18:56,200
To make sure readers
can relate to the heroine,

363
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:58,260
make her a bit of a klutz.

364
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:00,660
Then, with the appearance
of a rival in love,

365
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:02,600
the heroine agonizes alone.

366
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,860
They're almost together,
but they never quite get there.

367
00:19:04,860 --> 00:19:06,320
Argh, it's so frustrating!

368
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:08,620
If you like them, just say so already!

369
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:11,480
Just stirring up the
readers' feelings like that,

370
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,020
then a confession!

371
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:16,960
And then it turns out the transfer
student liked the hero from the start.

372
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,760
What a ridiculous development,

373
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:21,280
and it's perfectly fine to say so.

374
00:19:21,280 --> 00:19:23,360
Make the hero wear glasses,

375
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:25,680
and when he takes them off,
he's secretly handsome.

376
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:28,020
Do something like that,
and the readers will be even happier.

377
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:29,640
I see.

378
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,120
Next up is seinen manga.

379
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:37,140
The protagonist is a dull guy living alone.

380
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:40,600
Then a cute girl suddenly shows
up and ends up moving in with him.

381
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:44,400
If you write a story that fulfills
men's selfish fantasies like this,

382
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:46,220
readers will definitely bite.

383
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:51,400
Have the girl wear glasses and a maid outfit,
and they'll be even happier.

384
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:54,500
Next up is isekai fantasy manga.

385
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:57,320
Basically, it's a world where anything goes.

386
00:19:57,320 --> 00:20:02,520
Just say something vague like "psychic powers" or
"ages," and readers will accept it as just how things are.

387
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:06,680
But when anything goes, the story
can become totally incomprehensible.

388
00:20:06,680 --> 00:20:09,540
In that case, just label it
"End of Part One."

389
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,920
Mystery manga are based on tricks, but

390
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:16,520
before anyone can nitpick,
"Would the culprit really go to all that trouble?"

391
00:20:17,120 --> 00:20:19,300
bring up the culprit's sad backstory

392
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:22,100
and make everyone forget
about the far-fetched trick.

393
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:25,720
Somehow I feel like I could write one too.

394
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:26,420
Me too.

395
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:28,700
So, based on everything I've covered,

396
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:31,500
let's have you all actually draw some manga.

397
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:32,540
That said,

398
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:36,380
since amateurs like you won't
come up with ideas that easily,

399
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:39,280
I'll give you some
wonderful original stories.

400
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:41,300
*scribble scribble scribble*

401
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:43,320
Thank you very much.

402
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:47,380
A useless employee becomes
friends with the company president?

403
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:50,920
A submarine declares itself
an independent nation?

404
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:54,240
A hero with a bean-jam bun
for a face becomes a star?

405
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:57,280
A school time-travels to the future?

406
00:20:57,820 --> 00:21:00,520
A frog sticks to a
shirt after someone trips?

407
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,100
Robots fight each other?

408
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:05,680
Punishing evil in the name of the moon?

409
00:21:06,460 --> 00:21:11,180
Alright! Today's assignment is for each of you
to finish one manga based on one of those stories!

410
00:21:17,500 --> 00:21:20,600
All my characters end up
with the same face, though.

411
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:22,160
Just change their hairstyles.

412
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:24,840
I can't draw backgrounds well, though.

413
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:27,040
Just slap on a bunch of
screentone to cover it up.

414
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:29,800
Drawing the mechanical parts
one by one is such a pain.

415
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:31,200
Copy it, then flip and shrink it.

416
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:33,960
Looks like it's going to work out somehow.

417
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,360
As expected of Wara-san.

418
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:36,140
I'm done!

419
00:21:36,140 --> 00:21:36,760
Me too.

420
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:37,320
Me too.

421
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:41,040
Alright, once you're finished, put your
manuscripts on the lectern and you can go home.

422
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:45,340
Alright, that's all the manuscripts done.

423
00:21:45,340 --> 00:21:47,860
All that's left is printing them, right?

424
00:21:47,860 --> 00:21:50,400
Then I'll print ten
thousand copies right away.

425
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:51,680
Ten thousand, you hear?

426
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:53,340
Was that too many?

427
00:21:53,340 --> 00:21:55,960
Idiot! I'm saying it's too few!

428
00:21:57,340 --> 00:22:01,080
Popular manga magazines casually print over a million copies,
you know.

429
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:02,320
A million copies?

430
00:22:02,820 --> 00:22:06,080
Plus, this magazine carries
my super-popular manga,

431
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:08,720
Robo Deka Punch-R, too, you know.

432
00:22:09,340 --> 00:22:10,220
Three million?

433
00:22:10,220 --> 00:22:12,700
No, it'll sell five million copies.

434
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:18,360
Just wait, Weekly Sapphire,
for five million copies.

435
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:23,500
I'm going to sell every copy of the manga magazine I made and crush your magazine,
you hear me?

436
00:22:24,620 --> 00:22:29,140
So this is the Comic
Ryotsu that senpai made?

437
00:22:29,940 --> 00:22:32,420
So Robo Deka Bancho R is the Kanto one

438
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:34,740
As usual, the art is something else.

439
00:22:34,740 --> 00:22:36,980
It's even more something else with color.

440
00:22:36,980 --> 00:22:40,160
There's no way anyone would pick
up a manga like this from Kanto.

441
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:45,020
And the manga inside are all
things you've seen somewhere before.

442
00:22:45,020 --> 00:22:47,240
No one's going to buy a magazine like this.

443
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:49,400
Just as Reiko-san said.

444
00:22:50,120 --> 00:22:52,580
Comic Ryotsu,
which we printed five million copies of,

445
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:54,480
barely sold at all, you could say.

446
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:58,680
It wasn't Weekly Sapphire that went under.
It was this one.

447
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:02,480
There are too many people in this
world with no eye for quality.

448
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:04,720
No, no matter how you think about it,

449
00:23:04,720 --> 00:23:06,540
it's no wonder it didn't sell.

450
00:23:06,540 --> 00:23:07,800
Ryo-san,

451
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:09,980
the old man at Sekine Publishing

452
00:23:09,980 --> 00:23:10,620
Sensei,

453
00:23:10,620 --> 00:23:11,760
it's you.

454
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:13,080
Ryo-san!

455
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:16,520
Because of you, Ryo-san,
our company has finally gone bankrupt!

456
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,000
What are you going to do about it?

457
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,820
No, no, that's that's just...

458
00:23:19,820 --> 00:23:23,060
Sensei, what do you mean the
manga class is being shut down?

459
00:23:23,060 --> 00:23:26,820
I paid a whole year's tuition!
What are you going to do about that?

460
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:30,820
And you went and printed my manga in this
nonsensical magazine without my permission!

461
00:23:30,820 --> 00:23:31,680
This is fraud!

462
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:32,580
Seriously, that's so annoying!

463
00:23:32,580 --> 00:23:34,400
No, I mean this is...

464
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:35,120
This is - !

465
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:38,020
How could you, Ryo-san!

466
00:23:38,180 --> 00:23:38,280
Sensei!

467
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:41,900
Gah! Ryo-san!

468
00:23:42,580 --> 00:23:46,600
Wow! Manga magazines are
really going all out now!

469
00:23:49,700 --> 00:23:51,660
I don't want to, I don't want to!

470
00:23:51,780 --> 00:23:54,480
Why is it that I don't want
to do what I have to do,

471
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:56,880
yet I end up doing what I don't have to do!

472
00:23:57,060 --> 00:23:59,080
Maybe even the things I have to do,

473
00:23:59,100 --> 00:24:02,480
if someone tells me I don't have to,
I might suddenly want to!

474
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:05,460
I just don't wanna!

475
00:24:05,460 --> 00:24:07,460
One more, thanks!

476
00:24:08,420 --> 00:24:10,700
That place is Kameari

477
00:24:11,860 --> 00:24:14,420
Surely Kameari

478
00:24:14,420 --> 00:24:17,021
Everybody come on over,

479
00:24:17,071 --> 00:24:19,060
to our town

480
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:20,640
Thank you!

